    detail: "Sam directive (voice transcript 2026-06-15): 'Whenever I add new agents, they get the emails of the training courses as well as the email for Discord as well at the time of that 9:30 AM CST to log on with that Discord link.' Built end-to-end durable queue: (1) migration 20260615030443_agent_onboarding_email_queue.sql — public.agent_onboarding_queue table with UNIQUE(agent_id, email_kind) for idempotency, partial index on (target_send_at) WHERE sent_at IS NULL for cheap cron drains, RLS admin-only read/write (admin app_role), service_role bypass for the edge fn. fn_next_onboarding_window() computes the next 9:30 AM US/Central using `(date_trunc('day', now() AT TIME ZONE 'US/Central') + interval '9 hours 30 minutes')` projected back to UTC — CDT/CST handled automatically because we pivot via the timezone name not a hardcoded offset. fn_enqueue_agent_onboarding_emails() AFTER INSERT trigger on agents joins profiles via user_id to resolve email, RAISES NOTICE + RETURN NEW (skip silently, never block hiring) when email is missing, otherwise inserts course + discord rows ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING so trigger re-fires are safe. New trigger agents_after_insert_enqueue_onboarding ADDED to the existing 14-trigger chain on agents (Discord broadcast, Telegram new-hire, getting-started, ref-slug, etc all intact — verified pre-shipment with pg_get_triggerdef). (2) supabase/functions/send-agent-onboarding-email/index.ts — Deno serve drains queue rows where sent_at IS NULL AND target_send_at <= now() AND attempt_count < 5 (LIMIT 50 per fire). For each row joins agent.user_id → profiles for {email, full_name}, builds 'course' or 'discord' email (plain voice copy, no corporate larp — 'Hey {first_name}, ... — Sam'), POSTs to api.resend.com/emails with Bearer auth. NO FAKE SUCCESS — rejects HTML masquerade by requiring application/json content-type AND a string data.id field on the parsed body; anything else = fail + increment attempt_count + write last_error. On success writes sent_at + resend_message_id. (3) pg_cron — two schedules registered: apex-agent-onboarding-emails-cdt (jobid 53, '30 14 * * *' = 9:30 CDT) and apex-agent-onboarding-emails-cst (jobid 54, '30 15 * * *' = 9:30 CST). Both fire net.http_post into the edge fn with vault-decrypted apex_bot_token in Authorization header, mirroring the proven apex-insuracloud-sync-1m / apex-numbers-reminder pattern already used by 50+ APEX cron jobs. End-to-end verification (commit 1d38709f): force-enqueued 2 rows for Sam's existing agent (target_send_at = now() - 1s), curl-fired the edge fn, response {processed:2, sent:2, failed:0, errors:[]} — both Resend message IDs returned (16e7a82c-7555-49fe-914f-da708bd9748b, 9ce2a5de-7e99-453a-8bcb-137bd65088a9), test queue rows deleted after verification. CONFIGURATION OPEN: discord_invite_url row in system_settings is empty string (sentinel) — edge fn falls back to 'reply for invite' body copy until Sam sets the real Discord invite URL via UPDATE system_settings SET value='<url>' WHERE key='discord_invite_url'. system_settings rows seeded: discord_invite_url='', training_course_url='https://apex-financial.org/onboarding-course', onboarding_email_from_address='Sam James <sam@apex-financial.org>'. resend_api_key already lives in system_settings (re_NWgomMFC_...). Backfill SQL for the last 7 days of agents commented in the migration; uncomment + run via bot-sql if Sam wants existing recent agents to receive the emails on the next 9:30 AM CT fire. SWEEP-FOR-SAME-PATTERN: existing onboarding nudge sweep (onboarding-nudge-sweep edge fn) handles a different concern (multi-stage progress nudges) — this is just the day-zero send. Hold the Standard.",
